---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../data/content';
---

<Layout
  title="How texting with TenTo100 works"
  description="How TenTo100's SMS program works: how you opt in, what messages you'll receive, message frequency and rates, and how to opt out with STOP."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 py-16">
    <p class="eyebrow">SMS program</p>
    <h1 class="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">How messaging works</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
      How you join TenTo100's text program, what you'll receive, and how to stop anytime.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">How you join</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-accent-soft p-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">TenTo100's text line</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-ink">
          <strong>Text LESSON to [+1 (XXX) XXX-XXXX]</strong> — or just ask about or book a
          lesson in your own words. By texting, you agree to receive replies from TenTo100.
          Message frequency varies. Message &amp; data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out,
          HELP for help.
          Terms: <a class="text-accent underline" href="/terms">tento100.com/terms</a> &middot;
          Privacy: <a class="text-accent underline" href="/privacy">tento100.com/privacy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">The confirmation step — no messages until you say yes</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Before the program messages begin, the first text you receive is a one-time confirmation
        request, and it reads:
      </p>
      <blockquote class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-2 p-4 text-ink">
        “TenTo100: Reply YES to receive lesson scheduling and coaching texts. Msg frequency
        varies. Msg &amp; data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out, HELP for help. Terms:
        tento100.com/terms Privacy: tento100.com/privacy”
      </blockquote>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        <strong>If you do not reply YES, you will not receive program messages.</strong> Your
        consent — the exact language you agreed to, when, and on which channel — is recorded.
        You are never signed up silently, and joining is free.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What you'll receive</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Lesson scheduling and rescheduling, coaching follow-ups, and practice reminders from
        TenTo100 for clients who opt in. You will not receive unrelated marketing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Opting out and getting help</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to cancel — you'll get one confirmation and then
        no further messages. Reply <strong>HELP</strong>, or email
        <a class="text-accent underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, for help.
        Text START to rejoin.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequency and rates</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Message frequency varies based on your engagement with TenTo100. Message and data rates
        may apply, depending on your mobile carrier and plan. Mobile carriers are not liable for
        delayed or undelivered messages.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Privacy &amp; provider</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        We handle your information as described in our
        <a class="text-accent underline" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>; your mobile
        information and SMS consent are never shared with third parties or affiliates for
        marketing purposes. Full SMS program terms are in our
        <a class="text-accent underline" href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Messages are
        delivered through Twilio, our messaging provider. The program complies with the TCPA,
        CTIA Messaging Principles &amp; Best Practices, and A2P 10DLC requirements.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
